    "blurb": "The London show features a smoking Dark Star jam, a seamless Uncle John's Band → Wharf Rat transition and an inspired Good Lovin' performance. Jerry’s guitar shines throughout while the rhythm section drives the set with tight, propulsive playing. Recording quality is excellent despite the second‑set cut‑off.",
    "review": "The Strand Lyceum on May 25 1972 delivers a quintessential early‑’70s Dead experience. The first set builds steadily, culminating in a fiery Good Lovin' that showcases Jerry’s crystalline tone and Bob’s organ counterpoint. In the second set the band locks into a seamless Uncle John's Band → Wharf Rat segue before launching into an extended Dark Star where Phil’s soulful bass and Billy’s quick‑fire drumming underpin some of Garcia’s most inspired soloing of the era. The performance rolls forward into a soaring Sugar Magnolia and a heartfelt rendition of Sitting On Top Of The World, keeping the energy high until the tape fades after the finale.",
